---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import DoodleEllipse from '@components/DoodleEllipse.astro';
import photo from '@images/our_story/photo.webp';
---

<section
    id="story"
    class="section border-t border-charcoal"
    aria-labelledby="story-title"
>
    <div class="shell story__grid">
        <figure
            class="col-span-5 col-start-1"
            data-scroll="left"
        >
            <Image
                class="story__photo"
                alt="Leslie and Yolanda"
                densities={[1, 2]}
                src={photo}
                width={600}
            />
            <figcaption class="story__caption">Fig. 0.1 &mdash; Leslie &amp; Yolanda</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="col-span-6 col-start-7">
            <p
                class="eyebrow mb-12"
                data-scroll
            >
                Our story
            </p>
            <h2
                id="story-title"
                class="story__title"
                data-scroll
            >
                It started on a <span class="inline-block relative whitespace-nowrap">FaceTime call.<DoodleEllipse /></span>
            </h2>
            <div
                class="story__body"
                data-scroll
            >
                <p>The Figure Zero Project was founded by two high school friends, Leslie and Yolanda. Honestly, they didn't have a lot in common. Yolanda can be quite calm; Leslie, not so much. Despite this, they shared a similar passion for catching sunrises at Woodbine Beach, crying at the Eras Tour, hwachae, almost peeing their pants laughing at photobooths, and, most importantly, art.</p>
                <p>Although they eventually found themselves pursuing science, they found a way to bring art and scientific research together through the Figure Zero Project. Their journey began with illustrating journal covers, which soon expanded to a larger team that designs journal layouts and visual abstracts, and translates complex articles into words that anyone can understand. What started as an ordinary idea during a FaceTime call turned into a growing contribution to scientific communication. And they are only getting started.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    .story__body {
        color: var(--color-umber);
        font-size: 17px;
        line-height: 1.7;
        max-width: var(--measure-prose);
        text-wrap: pretty;
    }

    .story__body p:not(:last-child) {
        margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .story__body p:first-of-type::first-letter {
        float: left;
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-size: 64px;
        line-height: 0.8;
        padding: 6px 10px 0 0;
    }

    .story__caption {
        color: var(--color-taupe);
        font-family: var(--font-sans);
        font-size: 10px;
        letter-spacing: 0.16em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .story__grid {
        align-items: start;
        display: grid;
        gap: 24px;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
    }

    .story__photo {
        display: block;
        height: auto;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
        width: 100%;
    }

    .story__title {
        font-size: clamp(34px, calc(25.33px + 2.71vw), 60px);
        font-weight: 460;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        line-height: 1.05;
        margin-bottom: 48px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 1024px) {
        .story__grid {
            display: block;
        }

        .story__grid > * {
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }

        .story__grid > :last-child {
            margin-bottom: 0;
        }
    }
</style>
